1
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:06,200
Come out quickly.

2
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:20,220
If Pond finds out...

3
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:23,160
he's definitely going to tease me relentlessly, bro.

4
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:24,460
Then tease him back.

5
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,460
What's there to be afraid of? It's just Pond.

6
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:28,360
Um... so,

7
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,540
are you taking me out again today?

8
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,600
I do want to spend time just the two of us...

9
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:35,800
but Jae...

10
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,180
she's the one organizing the activity.

11
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,520
Sigh [sighs]

12
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:41,440
Alright, then.

13
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,740
In that case,

14
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,620
I'll find a nice restaurant and wait for you.

15
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:50,100
One more deposit.

16
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:55,400
A hug too.

17
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:57,240
Go on.

18
00:00:58,860 --> 00:00:59,900
Oh, it's hot.

19
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:00,420
Mm.

20
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:01,400
See you, bro. I...

21
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:02,780
uh, need to head over there now.

22
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,300
Did you think...

23
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:13,040
just because your friend owns a resort,

24
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:16,320
you can open any room whenever you want?

25
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,500
And here I thought I woke up early.

26
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:20,940
You're up pretty early too, Jae.

27
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:22,740
Do you like him?

28
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:26,300
Wait, you know?

29
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,460
The Boss knows too.

30
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:30,980
Khun Ton?

31
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:31,500
Yep.

32
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:35,040
Apparently, when we get back to Bangkok,

33
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,520
the Boss wants to see you.

34
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,360
The Boss called for me?

35
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:39,740
Mm-hmm.

36
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,300
Word has it...

37
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:45,240
the two of you...

38
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,460
are dating,

39
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:48,700
but it doesn't seem sincere.

40
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:50,120
Ton is dating Best...

41
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:53,580
just to heal his broken heart.

42
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,700
And Best is dating Ton...

43
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:56,460
because...

44
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,680
he's the company owner's younger brother.

45
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:00,320
Jae!

46
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:03,240
That's crazy! I didn't even know Tontae was Khun Ton's brother.

47
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:05,060
I only found out because you told me!

48
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:05,780
Oh?

49
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:07,540
Ton didn't tell you?

50
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,160
Ton didn't say anything.

51
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:12,040
We just started...

52
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:14,220
getting serious.

53
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,100
Oh, Best...

54
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:19,220
Jae...

55
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:19,780
Huh?

56
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,700
What should I do?

57
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,380
I think...

58
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:25,380
Khun Ton definitely doesn't like me.

59
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,280
Don't panic.

60
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:30,120
Don't overthink it yet.

61
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,960
Try talking to the Boss first and see what he says.

62
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:35,680
Then why didn't you tell me in the first place?

63
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,820
Well...

64
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,760
If I told you, would you two not fall for each other?

65
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,120
Could you really stop your feelings?

66
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,480
No.

67
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,560
Right?

68
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:47,380
Once we like someone,

69
00:02:47,380 --> 00:02:49,680
trying to suppress those feelings...

70
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:52,680
it just doesn't work, am I right?

71
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,600
Even me...

72
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,840
back when I lived in my provincial hometown,

73
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:00,080
I went out of my way to...

74
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,720
mince the meat,

75
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,040
make Larb,

76
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:05,040
and ride a motorized tricycle...

77
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,980
through sun and rain...

78
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:09,220
just to deliver it to a guy's house.

79
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:10,600
And do you know how it ended?

80
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,940
He gave that Larb to someone else to eat!

81
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,460
Just talking about it makes me furious.

82
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,560
Why does this story sound so familiar?

83
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,700
Huh?

84
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:19,500
Jae...

85
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:21,560
Try saying the name "Nan Krai".

86
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:24,100
Nan Krai.

87
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,900
P'Nan Krai...

88
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,680
I'm pretty sure it's them.

89
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:35,600
Why do I feel this weird sense of déjà vu?

90
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:39,180
Opportunity.

91
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:45,940
Whoa...

92
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:46,740
The sun is really scorching.

93
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:47,700
Yeah.

94
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,400
Tang-Oh.

95
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,160
Huh?

96
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:55,680
Did you talk to P'Dan about something?

97
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:58,020
Heyyy...

98
00:04:58,020 --> 00:04:59,780
Don't throw this on me, man.

99
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:03,760
P'Dan,

100
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,500
why are you sitting here?

101
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:08,200
N... Nothing really.

102
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,800
Some things...

103
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,160
you just have to let time handle.

104
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,080
You yourself...

105
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,780
can't control everything anyway, right?

106
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:21,920
Hey,

107
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:24,500
but you can control your own heart, man.

108
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,460
Whatever is complicated...

109
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,500
don't get your heart tangled up in it.

110
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:28,020
Tang-Oh.

111
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:28,940
What?

112
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,480
Uh... alright, alright.

113
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,200
Then,

114
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,960
just wait and see for now.

115
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,340
Try giving it a chance.

116
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:40,860
I think...

117
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:42,800
I'll give it a shot.

118
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:45,460
But do you think...

119
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:46,800
him and me...

120
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,440
are a good match?

121
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,120
I really don't know, man.

122
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,200
I don't know if...

123
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,660
him and I...

124
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,380
are suited for each other.

125
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:06,920
Man...

126
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:08,780
My friend...

127
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:13,400
If you love someone, but in the end...

128
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,640
there's no future together,

129
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,340
should you still keep loving them?

130
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:16,860
Yeah...

131
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,400
If you love them, but know it leads nowhere...

132
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,080
should I start giving up on them?

133
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:31,280
Yeah, let's be sad together, buddy.

134
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,880
It's so depressing.

135
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,320
I get you, man.

136
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,900
I understand.

137
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,460
Are you really serious about this?

138
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:51,040
Hey... hold on, bro.

139
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,160
Don't tell me...

140
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,900
you're getting back with that kid?

141
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,540
Well, he asked me for a chance.

142
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:06,880
But as for me...

143
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:09,760
will I really have a chance to stand by his side?

144
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,160
But... when you were alone,

145
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:16,400
you did just fine without him, didn't you?

146
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,360
That's true.

147
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:23,020
Don't tell me...

148
00:07:23,020 --> 00:07:24,500
that you miss him?

149
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,920
Who said...

150
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,020
I missed him?

151
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:29,180
*Sigh*...

152
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:36,580
But you know what?

153
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,800
When I was over there...

154
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,320
I missed you so damn much.

155
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:43,820
What's wrong with you?

156
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:45,620
Should we pop it open now, bro?

157
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:46,760
Hey!

158
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,880
Pop what open?

159
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:48,760
Let's go.

160
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,240
How can you be so sure...

161
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:03,420
that he genuinely loves you?

162
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:05,780
Does he really want to build a life with you?

163
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,380
Well, he...

164
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:10,240
He said...

165
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:12,860
he sees me in his future.

166
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:18,940
*Sigh* Whatever.

167
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:22,640
He's telling you everything you've always wanted to hear.

168
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:24,480
Who could resist that?

169
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,460
You need to root for me.

170
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,700
Cheer me up.

171
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:33,840
Cheer me up.

172
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:36,620
Cheer me up.

173
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,180
Fine.

174
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:41,560
I'll cheer for you.

175
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,240
Didn't you say last night that you were done with him?

176
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:01,500
That's what I thought too.

177
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,660
I think...

178
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:09,760
Should you find someone new, bro?

179
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:12,700
Someone like you...

180
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:15,140
if you go out there, you can find plenty of people.

181
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:18,520
A moment ago, you were rooting for him like crazy.

182
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:21,180
I wasn't rooting for him,

183
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,820
I was rooting for you.

184
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:25,220
I just thought you were just having fun.

185
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,160
That's you, not me.

186
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,860
Wait, bro...

187
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:37,400
Since when did you fall so hard for P'Dan that you can't look at anyone else?

188
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:38,620
Since when?

189
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:41,260
You've only been dating for a few months,

190
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:43,180
and you're already head over heels...

191
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,620
completely hooked.

192
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,660
Who told you it's only been a few months?

193
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,220
Here.

194
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,920
Take it.

195
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,600
Hey... no way.

196
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,980
What are you staring at?

197
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:35,480
Oh...

198
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,800
Staring at the student council president, I see.

199
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,940
My, my...

200
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:42,260
Uh...

201
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:43,800
I was staring at the tree branch.

202
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,480
What are you talking about?

203
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,160
Look at that!

204
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,100
Whoa...

205
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,460
Your eyes were locked right on him.

206
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:53,140
I'm pretty sure he knows you were looking.

207
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,220
Like hell he knows!

208
00:10:56,940 --> 00:10:58,260
Whoa... he's looking back!

209
00:10:58,260 --> 00:10:59,460
Your Mr. President!

210
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,440
He's not mine!

211
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,160
Act shy, go ahead!

212
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:07,640
So bold for a 10th grader to fall for a 12th grader!

213
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:10,480
I never said I liked him!

214
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:11,000
Really?

215
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:12,660
Hey, bro, bro!

216
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:17,740
Man, but you can only admire from afar.

217
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:18,740
No point in liking him now.

218
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,360
Look at his boyfriend, see that?

219
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,640
Yeah... I'll just keep watching then.

220
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,740
Keep admiring, then!

221
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:32,240
You have to compete with his ex now.

222
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:34,800
I already wished for him to be biased toward me.

223
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:35,600
Whoa...

224
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:37,580
Well, I hope he really is biased toward you.

225
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,360
Girl...

226
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,900
I'm sure of what I saw last night.

227
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:58,660
What was it?

228
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,820
Best and Tae didn't sleep in the same room,

229
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:04,320
but this morning, they walked each other to the front of the room! Ooh!

230
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:07,660
Just this is enough to make me explode with joy!

231
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:08,280
Right?

232
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:10,480
I couldn't fan-girl any harder than this.

233
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,340
Definitely not!

234
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:12,640
What about the other couples?

235
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:13,740
Uh... wait a sec.

236
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:14,760
Let me picture it.

237
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,320
If it were Pond and Dan...

238
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,500
Honestly, no way, girl.

239
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:25,280
They don't match at all. It doesn't work.

240
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:28,440
Whoa...

241
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:31,280
Ladies!

242
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:36,340
Are you two still not done ship-proofing those couples?

243
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:38,540
Ladies...

244
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:40,360
Still at it, you two?

245
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:42,240
Hey,

246
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,600
what if someone told you

247
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:47,420
that the two of you aren't suited to be friends?

248
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:49,600
Would you stop being friends right away?

249
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:52,000
Come on, Jae!

250
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,760
We're just... like...

251
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,940
Look over there, Jae! See for yourself!

252
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:59,340
Oh?

253
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,420
Whoa, girl!

254
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:06,860
It actually works!

255
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:07,920
Not bad at all!

256
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,020
Pond-Dan!

257
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:10,780
It works!

258
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:11,840
"It works" as in...

259
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,140
totally works!

260
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:14,680
Our office will have both...

261
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:15,740
Best-Tae,

262
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,480
Pond-Dan!

263
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,000
And what about us?

264
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,280
Aoy-Jan, of course!

265
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,820
Does that even work? [laughter]

266
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,200
Besties!

267
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,020
Does this count? / The trouble-making duo!

268
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:28,160
It works!

269
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:28,640
Right?

270
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:29,600
It works as in...

271
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,820
"works" meaning...

272
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:32,820
kind of works!

273
